{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1511071-the-all-consuming-lantern","id":1511071,"title":"The All-Consuming Lantern","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-08T07:11:35-07:00","id":1511071,"title":"The All-Consuming Lantern","content":"This idea came to me while in the shower on a sick day off from work to take care of an important errand (someone went around slashing the tires of cars in my apartment complex's parking lot on Saturday night, and all the auto shops in town are closed on Sunday). It's a small hack to make Obsessions meatier and more, well, obsessional for characters. If using this hack, I would encourage players to at least consider taking more longterm-style Obsessions, greater Mysteries that can't be resolved with a single Scrutiny.<br /> <br /> <b>Obsessions</b><ul><li><b>The Shining Path:</b> In addition to the normal mechanical effects from the corebook, all Obsessions a mage possesses also come with their own instance of the Obsession Condition. The bonus and penalty from the Condition apply to mundane rolls only (but see below). The Condition fades without resolving if the mage drops or solves the Obsession, and the player chooses whether the Condition grants normal or Arcane Beats when triggered.</li> <li><b>Supernal Focus:</b> A mage's Obsessions are never penalized by unrelated Obsession Conditions, whether mystical or mundane.</li> <li><b>A Beautiful Mind:</b> A mage with multiple Obsession slots can dedicate more than one to a single Obsession. With two slots, the Obsession Condition grants the 8-again quality on related rolls. With three slots, three successes on a related roll counts as an exceptional success (in addition to 8-again). With four slots, related rolls enjoy the rote quality. Each dedicated Obsession slot beyond the first imposes a -1 penalty to unrelated non-magical rolls.</li> <li><b>Clarity of Purpose:</b> When Scrutinizing a Mystery, a mage adds the number of Obsession slots dedicated to the Mystery to the total number of safe rolls she can make before risking corruption. For example, a mage who has dedicated three Obsession slots to &quot;The Arcadian Verge on Maple Street&quot; has three extra safe rolls when Scrutinizing said Verge. This can retroactively contaminate a Mystery if during the middle of an investigation a mage somehow loses an Obsession.</li> <li><b>Obsessive Will:</b> When casting spells in pursuit of an Obsession (such as a Knowing spell to reveal important information about a Mystery, or a Ruling spell to keep an aggressive spirit out of the mage's way while Scrutinizing), a mage can use their Obsession as a Yantra, providing a Yantra bonus equal to its dedicated slots. For the purposes of spells like As Above, So Below, each individual Obsession counts as a unique Yantra. Drawing on one's Supernal desires leaves an imprint in the Nimbus, however; that the spell is related to a mage's Obsession becomes Surface Information for anyone Scrutinizing the effect (or Deep Information if cast as a rote).</li> <li><b>Antinomian Defilement:</b> Scelesti of Nasnas initiation and higher can befoul not just their own spells, but the Obsessions of other mages as well. More to come on this later. . .</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-08T07:25:24-07:00","id":1511072,"title":"","content":"Nice. The first quality/hack even sounds like one of those \u201cWait, it wasn\u2019t official?\u201d hacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T17:03:44-07:00","id":1511165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1511071-the-all-consuming-lantern?p=1511072#post1511072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice. The first quality/hack even sounds like one of those \u201cWait, it wasn\u2019t official?\u201d hacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I even had to go double-check the book to make sure I wasn't misremembering that. What I <i>did</i> misremember was how the Obsession Condition works, which is why some of this is written a little awkwardly to smooth out an original mechanical error.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T17:57:33-07:00","id":1511169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1511071-the-all-consuming-lantern?p=1511072#post1511072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice. The first quality/hack even sounds like one of those \u201cWait, it wasn\u2019t official?\u201d hacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure how I'd go about tracking down the post, but I'm like 90% certain Dave mentioned that at one point in 2e's development Obsessions imposed the Obsession Condition a la Rotes and the rote action quality being not-coincidentally named in 1e.<br /> <br /> <br /> Important question: how does stacking Obsessions interact with effects that rewrite Obsessions, whether from spells or from the Conditions imposed by an Act of Hubris?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T18:09:05-07:00","id":1511171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1511071-the-all-consuming-lantern?p=1511169#post1511169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure how I'd go about tracking down the post, but I'm like 90% certain Dave mentioned that at one point in 2e's development Obsessions imposed the Obsession Condition a la Rotes and the rote action quality being not-coincidentally named in 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. Makes sense.<br /> <br /> I wonder if we can somehow make the way-too-wordy \u201cachieves an exceptional success at three successes instead of five\u201d dice trick\u2019s name key off Praxes too. (Or the Inspired Condition) Food for thought later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Important question: how does stacking Obsessions interact with effects that rewrite Obsessions, whether from spells or from the Conditions imposed by an Act of Hubris? </div> </div> </div>Not the OP obviously, but I suspect the bonuses/penalties just scale down normally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T16:46:19-07:00","id":1511299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1511071-the-all-consuming-lantern?p=1511169#post1511169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Important question: how does stacking Obsessions interact with effects that rewrite Obsessions, whether from spells or from the Conditions imposed by an Act of Hubris?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd have to meditate on that a bit more, but my first instinct is that an Obsession slot can be overwritten in that case. That actually opens the possibility of, say, Rampant's Obsession stacking in certain cases. Yes, I'll definitely have to think about that more (and the &quot;Become Wiser&quot; Obsession as well).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-16T07:36:47-07:00","id":1511801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1511071-the-all-consuming-lantern#post1511071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li><b>Clarity of Purpose:</b> When Scrutinizing a Mystery, a mage adds the number of Obsession slots dedicated to the Mystery to the total number of safe rolls she can make before risking corruption. For example, a mage who has dedicated three Obsession slots to &quot;The Arcadian Verge on Maple Street&quot; has three extra safe rolls when Scrutinizing said Verge. <b>This can retroactively contaminate a Mystery if during the middle of an investigation a mage somehow loses an Obsession.</b></li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a huge pain to storytell, I'd remove the bolded part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13248-jsnider3","name":"jsnider3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}